+    // SleepThread calls whose caller returns to 0x100afa8 -- the loop's own `lbu $v1,0x0($s0)` -- but
+    // only ONE watched read at that pc, so the polled byte must be at an address the enumerated set
+    // never covered. A range has no blind spot: 0x70002060..0x700020A0 covers stride 12 (0x6D/79/85/
+    // 91), stride 16 (0x6D/7D/8D/9D) and everything in between.
+    return a >= 0x70002060u && a <= 0x700020A0u;
